    "body": "Around a month ago [xonsh become 0.9.20](https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/releases/tag/0.9.20) with this:\r\n\r\n> Support for ANSI escape codes in $PROMPT/$RIGHT_PROMPT. In this way 3rd party prompt generators like powerline or starship can be used to set the prompt. ANSI escape codes might be mixed with the normal formatting (like {BOLD_GREEN}) and prompt variables (like {user}) should work as well.\r\nFor example:\r\n> $PROMPT=lambda: $(starship prompt)\r\n\r\nHere the PRs:\r\n* https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/pull/3690 (released in 0.9.20)\r\n* https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/pull/3781 (moved to the next PR)\r\n* https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/pull/3784 (merged to master but not released yet)\r\n\r\nI've tested on Linux and it works:\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20200919_163410](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1708680/93668597-f672a100-fa95-11ea-96cf-ed945b2a451f.png)\r\n\r\n@vladimyr Is it resolved the issue? If yes could you please continue working on #1265? I can help with testing on linux.",
